# Second line of defence only. The real guarantee is the Dockerfile's explicit COPY
# allowlist -- a file no COPY names cannot reach a layer whatever this file says.
# What this file buys is a smaller build context and a secret that never leaves the
# working tree for the daemon in the first place.
#
# The Build Context does NOT read .gitignore, so every rule is restated here.

# Credentials and keys, in every spelling this repo or a developer might use.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
_netrc
credentials*.json
id_rsa*
*.keystore

.git
.gitignore
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
dist
.tmp-ux-validation
.working

# Agent/BMAD tooling and planning artifacts: not application code, and several of
# them are machine-specific.
.agents
.claude
.codex
.bmad-loop
_bmad
_bmad-output

# The Image runs the app; it does not run the suite. Playwright is a dev dependency
# and `uv sync --no-dev` leaves it out, so the Browser tests could not run anyway.
tests
docs
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
deploy
mvp.md
plan.md
